Day -1 quick Revsion on arrays for DSA
What Is an Array?
An array is a collection of elements stored in contiguous memory locations and accessed using indexing. All elements are of the same data type.

Commonly Used Methods with Time Complexity
Arrays.sort(array)	Sorts the entire array (ascending order by default)	O(n log n)
Arrays.sort(array, fromIndex, toIndex)	Sorts a subarray	O(k log k), k = (toIndex - fromIndex)
Arrays.binarySearch(array, key)	Searches for key in sorted array	O(log n)
Arrays.binarySearch(array, fromIndex, toIndex, key)	Searches for key in subarray	O(log k)
Arrays.equals(arr1, arr2)	Compares two arrays for equality	O(n)
Arrays.toString(array)	Converts array to a readable string	O(n)
Arrays.fill(array, val)	Fills the entire array with a value	O(n)
Arrays.fill(array, fromIndex, toIndex, val)	Fills part of the array	O(k), k = (toIndex - fromIndex)
Arrays.copyOf(array, newLength)	Copies array to a new array with desired length	O(min(n, newLength))
Arrays.copyOfRange(array, from, to)	Copies part of array	O(k)
Arrays.setAll(array, lambda)	Sets each element using a generator function	O(n)
Arrays.stream(array)	Converts array to a Stream (Java 8+)	O(1)
Arrays.deepEquals(arr1, arr2)	Compares nested arrays	O(n) recursively
Arrays.deepToString(arr)	Converts nested arrays to string	O(n) recursively
Arrays.asList(array)	Converts array to fixed-size List	O(1)


Example 
Arrays.copyOf() and Arrays.copyOfRange()
int[] a = {1, 2, 3};
int[] b = Arrays.copyOf(a, 5);       // [1, 2, 3, 0, 0]
int[] c = Arrays.copyOfRange(a, 1, 3); // [2, 3]

 Arrays.asList() – Fixed-size List (backed by the array)
String[] fruits = {"apple", "banana"};
List<String> list = Arrays.asList(fruits);  // Changes in list affect array

| Category       | Methods                                                |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Sorting**    | `sort(arr)`, `sort(arr, from, to)`                     |
| **Searching**  | `binarySearch(arr, key)`                               |
| **Comparison** | `equals()`, `deepEquals()`                             |
| **Copying**    | `copyOf()`, `copyOfRange()`, `System.arraycopy()`      |
| **Filling**    | `fill()`, `setAll()`                                   |
| **Conversion** | `toString()`, `deepToString()`, `asList()`, `stream()` |

Performance Tips for DSA Prep

Use Arrays.sort() when required — optimized with TimSort (hybrid of merge + insertion sort).

Avoid Arrays.asList() if you need a flexible list.

Use System.arraycopy() for performance-critical array copy (lower-level, faster than copyOf()).


